<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 439)</h2>
<p><b>Compare sides now decode as themselves.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Comparing a Rec.709 QuickTime against an ACEScg EXR? Each side gets its own input transform: the B side uses its declared space, or the remembered default for <b>its</b> kind of file — never A's transform by accident.</li>
<li>To set B's space explicitly, put the working side on B (the A|B toggle) and pick from the input menu — the pipeline popover reads <b>Input · B</b> while it routes there. Playlist clips keep the choice with the session; A's setting is never touched. Frame grabs follow.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
